# Review: LaMetricPlugin

The plugin is built to the spec and unusually well tested. Frame projection (`toFrames`), the four-frame cap,
indexed frames, abbreviated stat labels, local and cloud transports, DIY widget discovery and the
de-duplicating, trailing-edge `Pusher` all have unit tests, and `smoke.test.ts` drives the local transport
against a stand-in HTTP device. Gaps are at the edges. `PushStatus` on failure never carries the HTTP
`status`: the transport throws a plain `Error` and the pusher reports only `{ state: 'failed' }`. The
settings schema has no `port` or `scheme` field, so the user cannot pick plain HTTP or a non-default port
though `TransportConfig` supports both. The Tauri HTTP permission allows any host on ports 8080 and 4343, not
only LaMetric hosts. The headless driver itself (`dashboard-driver.ts`) has no test.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

